<article class="env-lemma" id="46CE93">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/46CE93">Lemma <span data-tag="46CE93">6.4.4.8</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be a presentable $\infty $-category in which colimits are universal, and let $f: \emptyset \rightarrow X$ be a morphism in $\calX $, where $\emptyset $ is an initial object of $\calX $. Then $f$ is a monomorphism. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $Y$ be an arbitrary object of $\calX $, we wish to show that composition with $f$ induces a $(-1)$-truncated map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \bHom _{\calX }( Y, \emptyset ) \rightarrow \bHom _{\calX }(Y, X). \]
</div>
    <p>
       If $Y$ is an initial object of $\calX $, then both sides are contractible; otherwise the left side is empty (Lemma <a href="/tag/0FD9C4" data-tag="0FD9C4">6.1.3.6</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>